      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Houston",
      "description": "The adjunct nursing role is a non-tenure track position with primary responsibility to provide adjunct instruction in the BSN program, clinically-focused MSN programs and the DNP program. The nursing faculty role reflects the philosophy and organizational standards of the larger university as well as those of the profession of nursing. Adjunct faculty members are expected to demonstrate productivity and competency consistent with their singular role of teaching, with assignments reflecting an emphasis on clinical instruction within the adjunct’s area of clinical specialization.",
