      "description": "The Clinical Teaching Assistant (CTA) provides direct support to lead clinical faculty in the instruction and supervision of nursing students during lab and clinical rotations. This position exists to enhance the student-to-instructor ratio, support individualized learning, and ensure a safe and high-quality clinical learning environment. CTAs facilitate the development of clinical skills, critical thinking, and professional behavior in alignment with program objectives. Work is performed under general supervision, with duties aligned to established procedures and instructional goals. Performance is evaluated based on the successful support of clinical instruction and student progress, in accordance with University policies.",
